theory.intro:
Two simple summaries describe a data display: the **range** (how spread out the values are) and the **mode** (the value that appears most often).
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(8.8,0);
\foreach \x in {0,...,8} {\draw (\x,0.08)--(\x,-0.08); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.08) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,2/2,3/4,4/2,6/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.34*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\draw[<->] (1,-0.7)--(6,-0.7) node[midway,below,font=\small] {range: largest $-$ smallest};
\node[above,font=\small] at (3,1.5) {mode: tallest stack};
\node[below] at (4,-1.7) {Value};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
The dot plot shows the number of books read by a group of students. Find the range and mode.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (-0.4,0)--(8.4,0);
\foreach \x in {0,...,8} {\draw[black] (\x,0.08)--(\x,-0.08); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.08) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {2/1,3/2,4/4,5/2,7/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill[black] (\x,{0.4*\k}) circle (2pt);}}
\node[below] at (4,-0.65) {Number of books};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The dot plots show the number of goals scored in games by two teams. Find all modes for each team.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.7cm,y=0.7cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\foreach \b/\name in {0/Team A,3/Team B} {
\draw[black] (-0.4,\b)--(6.4,\b);
\foreach \x in {0,...,6} {\draw[black] (\x,{\b+0.08})--(\x,{\b-0.08}); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,{\b-0.08}) {$\x$};}
\node[above] at (3,{\b+1.7}) {\name};}
\foreach \x in {1,...,5} {\fill[black] (\x,0.4) circle (2pt);}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,2/3,3/1,4/3,5/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill[black] (\x,{3+0.4*\k}) circle (2pt);}}
\node[below] at (3,-0.65) {Goals scored};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The dot plots show the number of cups sold each hour at two stalls. Compare their ranges and all their modes. How much greater is the larger range? Which stall has more consistent sales?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\foreach \b/\name in {0/Stall A,3.4/Stall B} {
\draw[black] (-0.4,\b)--(9.4,\b);
\foreach \x in {0,...,9} {\draw[black] (\x,{\b+0.08})--(\x,{\b-0.08}); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,{\b-0.08}) {$\x$};}
\node[above] at (4.5,{\b+1.8}) {\name};}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,4/3,6/3,9/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill[black] (\x,{0.4*\k}) circle (2pt);}}
\foreach \x/\c in {3/1,5/2,6/4,7/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill[black] (\x,{3.4+0.4*\k}) circle (2pt);}}
\node[below] at (4.5,-0.65) {Cups sold per hour};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

