mastery.question_text:
The paired dot plots show two runners' practice times, in seconds.
Compare their ranges and modes, and decide which runner is more consistent.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.78]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(9.3,0); \draw[->] (-0.5,2.7)--(9.3,2.7);
\foreach \i in {0,...,17} {\draw ({0.5*\i},0.08)--({0.5*\i},-0.08); \draw ({0.5*\i},2.78)--({0.5*\i},2.62);}
\foreach \x/\v in {0/11.9,1.5/12.2,3/12.5,4.5/12.8,6/13.1,7.5/13.4,8.5/13.6} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize,rotate=90,anchor=east] at (\x,-0.12) {$\v$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize,rotate=90,anchor=east] at (\x,2.58) {$\v$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {1.5/1,3/2,4.5/1,6/2,7.5/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\foreach \x/\c in {0/1,3/3,6/1,8.5/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{2.7+0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[left] at (-0.55,0.8) {Runner A}; \node[left] at (-0.55,3.5) {Runner B}; \node[below] at (4.25,-1.7) {Time (seconds)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The paired dot plots show the times, in seconds, taken to complete a puzzle.
A student says that Set S has a larger mode and a larger range than Set R.
Evaluate the claim.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.78]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(10.5,0); \draw[->] (-0.5,2.7)--(10.5,2.7);
\foreach \x/\v in {0/20.9,1/21.4,3.4/22.6,4.6/23.2,6.4/24.1,7.6/24.7,8.8/25.3,9.8/25.8} {\draw (\x,0.08)--(\x,-0.08); \draw (\x,2.78)--(\x,2.62); \node[below,font=\scriptsize,rotate=90,anchor=east] at (\x,-0.12) {$\v$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize,rotate=90,anchor=east] at (\x,2.58) {$\v$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,3.4/2,6.4/2,9.8/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\foreach \x/\c in {0/1,4.6/3,7.6/1,8.8/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{2.7+0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[left] at (-0.55,0.8) {Set R}; \node[left] at (-0.55,3.5) {Set S}; \node[below] at (4.9,-1.7) {Time (seconds)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
